1. Allowed without permission.
   Viewing and reading the source code and documentation on GitHub, and forking within GitHub to the
   extent required by the GitHub Terms of Service for public repositories, without running the software
   or using the code outside GitHub.

2. Allowed only with the copyright holder's prior written permission.
   - running, installing or using the software or any part of it;
   - copying the code outside GitHub;
   - modifying the code or creating derivative works;
   - distributing, publishing, sublicensing or selling it;
   - any commercial use, including internal company use or use in services;
   - using the code, documentation or texts to train or fine-tune AI models.

3. How to ask for permission.
   Open an Issue titled "Permission request / Запрос разрешения" at https://github.com/Mybrohugs/jarvis
   or contact @Mybrohugs on GitHub. Say who you are and what you want to use, and for what. Permission
   is valid only when the copyright holder gives it in writing (in the Issue or a message). It may be
   limited in scope, time and conditions, and it is not transferable.

4. Third-party components.
   Third-party libraries, models, fonts and services used by the project remain under their own licenses
   and terms (see NOTICE.md). This license does not apply to them.

5. No warranty.
   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The copyright holder is not liable
   for any damage arising from its use, including permitted use.

6. Termination.
   Any breach of these terms automatically terminates all permissions granted.

